# Claude Desktop instances.
#
#   name | bundle id | profile dir | icon hue (degrees) | env (optional)
#
# env        optional KEY=VALUE pairs, separated by ';', exported before the app
#            starts. A .app does NOT inherit your shell environment, so this is
#            the only way to give an instance its own CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR -- which
#            is what Claude Code (including the desktop app's agent mode) reads
#            hooks from. Leading ~ is expanded.
#
# name       becomes the app "/Applications/Claude <name>.app" and its selector
#            (lowercased) for claude-apps-refresh.sh
# bundle id  must be unique per instance; changing it later forces a re-login
# profile    each instance MUST have its own; two instances sharing one profile
#            can corrupt it
# hue        0 red · 30 orange · 55 yellow · 142 green · 175 teal · 212 blue
#            · 275 purple · 320 pink   (icon is generated on first build)
#
# Add a line, run `claude-apps-refresh.sh`, and the new instance is built.

Personal   | com.example.claude-personal   | ~/Library/Application Support/Claude            | 142 |
Enterprise | com.example.claude-enterprise | ~/Library/Application Support/Claude-Enterprise | 212 | CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude-work
